        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): preserve emoji in tool detail previews",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Android pending-tool detail previews would show malformed Unicode when a tool argument's first line placed an emoji across the 160-code-unit truncation boundary.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPending-tool detail previews truncate the first line at 157 UTF-16 code units before appending an ellipsis. That chokepoint now reuses the existing Android `takeUtf16Safe` helper (same helper already used for app session labels and notification text) so a split surrogate pair is dropped instead of rendered. The 160-code-unit size contract is unchanged.\n\nTo avoid inventing a new native i18n source template, truncation is bound to a local `preview` and rendered with the existing `$preview…` pattern. `native:i18n:sync` / locale artifacts / `android-app-i18n sync` remove the obsolete `${firstLine.take(157)}…` inventory entry and unused `native_09f0bda624faadd4` resources (net −1 inventory entry).\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `ToolDisplay`, `takeUtf16Safe`, `preserve emoji` / UTF-16 Android tool preview; no competing open PR on this surface. Closest landed siblings: #108102 (session labels), #108101 / #108103 (Android UTF-16 status/reason paths).\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before:** an emoji landing on the 157-code-unit cut could leave a lone high surrogate in the pending-tool detail line.\n- **After:** the preview stays well-formed Unicode; arguments that do not cross the limit render exactly as before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Exact head: `68c5ed4f8c2762a0ddceb66d8016a494f8ea3eaa`\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n- `node --import tsx scripts/native-app-i18n.ts check` — passed (`changed=false`)\n- `node --import tsx scripts/android-app-i18n.ts check` — passed\n- Focused regression: `ToolDisplayRegistryTest.resolvePreservesUtf16BoundariesAtDetailPreviewLimit` (split + complete emoji at the 157-unit cut via `ToolDisplayRegistry.resolve` / `bash`+`command`)\n- Hosted CI proof:\n  - `android-test-play` PASS — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29422003591/job/87374794646 (`BUILD SUCCESSFUL`, includes `ToolDisplayRegistryTest`)\n  - `android-test-third-party` PASS — same workflow\n  - `native-i18n` PASS — https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29422003591/job/87374794253\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n### Production string operations (mirrors Kotlin String.take / Character.isHighSurrogate)\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx proof-android-tool-display-utf16.mts\n```\n\n```\nnode=v22.22.0\ninput.length=162 (156 prefix + 2-char emoji + 4-char 'tail')\ninput[156]=U+d83d (high surrogate)\ninput[157]=U+de00 (low surrogate)\n\n=== Case 1: negative control (raw take) ===\n  result.length=157\n  result last code=U+d83d\n  isHighSurrogate(last)=true\n  ok: take(157) returns 157 code units\n  ok: take(157) ends on a high surrogate (malformed Unicode)\n  ok: take(157) drops the low surrogate\n\n=== Case 2: positive control (takeUtf16Safe) ===\n  result.length=156\n  result last code=U+61\n  ok: takeUtf16Safe(157) returns ≤157 code units\n  ok: takeUtf16Safe(157) does NOT end on a high surrogate\n  info: dropped emoji=true safe_len=156\n\n=== Case 3: complete emoji fits ===\n  result.length=157\n  contains emoji=true\n  ok: takeUtf16Safe(157) keeps the emoji when it fits\n  ok: result starts with 155 a's prefix\n\n=== Case 4: visual HTML proof ===\n  html=/tmp/proof-tool-display-utf16.html\n  screenshot=/tmp/proof-tool-display-utf16.png (42327 bytes)\n  ok: headless Chrome produced a PNG screenshot\n\n=== Summary ===\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 8 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n### Visual rendering proof (headless Chrome, monospace matching Android FontFamily.Monospace)\n\nThe `proof-android-tool-display-utf16.mts` script renders the before/after text in a dark-themed monospace HTML page (mirroring the Android tool bubble styling) and captures it via `google-chrome --headless --screenshot`. The 800×520 PNG shows:\n\n- **❌ BEFORE** (`String.take(157)`): text ends at a lone high surrogate U+D83D — Compose Text will render a tofu/box character\n- **✅ AFTER split** (`takeUtf16Safe(157)`): emoji cleanly dropped at boundary, text is well-formed Unicode\n- **✅ AFTER complete** (`takeUtf16Safe(157)` with 155-char prefix): 😀 fits under the 157-unit cap and is preserved intact\n\nThe script file is at the repo root: `proof-android-tool-display-utf16.mts`\n\n### Robolectric boundary test (Android JVM, real Kotlin tool display logic)\n\n`ToolDisplayRegistryTest.resolvePreservesUtf16BoundariesAtDetailPreviewLimit`:\n\n- Calls `ToolDisplayRegistry.resolve()` with `name=\"bash\"`, `command=\"<156 a's>😀tail\"`\n- Asserts `detail == \"<156 a's>…\"` (no high surrogate at end)\n- Confirms the complete-emoji case keeps `😀` intact\n\n### Mutation check\n\n- Revert `takeUtf16Safe` → `take` in `ToolDisplay.kt:210` → test fails with high surrogate assertion\n- Restore fix → test passes\n\n### What was not tested\n\n- Physical Android device/emulator pending-tool row screenshot (no Android SDK or KVM in proof environment)\n- The headless Chrome rendering visual proof demonstrates identical string behavior in a monospace rendering context\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\n\nLow. Reuses an existing Android helper at one display chokepoint; size contract unchanged. i18n sync only removes an obsolete tracked template that was not a user-facing translation. Mitigation: Robolectric boundary test + hosted `android-test-play` / `native-i18n` + standalone proof script.\n\nAI-assisted change; no agent transcript attached.",
